# NLSY79 subset — SES & race effects on educational attainment, with vs without academic characteristics

**Data**: data/nls_raw.csv, n=12,686 (ages 14–22 in 1979), 61 cols.
**Outcome proxy**: "Highest grade completed, 1979" (0–20 yrs), standardized; cohort is 14–22 so this measures **early attainment**, not eventual BA completion (only n=39 have ≥16 yrs; BA-proxy reported but not used in conclusions).
**SES (family of origin)**: composite z-index (SESz) = mean of standardized log 1979 family income, mother's and father's education, pro/managerial father-figure occupation, negative family size (any 4 of 5 components). Individual indicators also modeled.
**Race**: Black =1, Hispanic =2 vs Non-Black/Non-Hispanic =3 (ref). **Academic**: ASVAB composite (mean of 4 standardized subtest z-scores); class-standing percentile (1 − rank/class size) secondary.

## Sample sizes
Composite sample S1 n=9,310 (race+sex+age+SESz+asvab); individual-indicator sample n=5,531; class-rank subsample n=4,546 (structurally missing, in-school only).

